# Carry this machine's extraction verdicts into mosaic's pii_extraction_status.
# Off the per-bin path on purpose: four machines write to that table and one
# updates millions of rows at a time, so a small UPDATE can queue behind it for
# minutes. Batching a few hours' verdicts takes that lock a handful of times a
# day instead of a dozen times an hour.
#
# Nothing depends on this running promptly -- the queue build anti-joins against
# agentic_extraction_status, so work already done is skipped whether or not
# mosaic's table knows yet. This is for progress read from mosaic's side.
#
# Absolute paths throughout: cron starts in $HOME, not the repo.
0 */4 * * * PROJECT_ID=cio-mosaic-analytics-pr-853ae3 PYTHONPATH=/home/jupyter/agentic-extraction-engine /opt/micromamba/bin/python3 /home/jupyter/agentic-extraction-engine/scripts/sync_status_to_mosaic.py --apply >> /home/jupyter/agentic-extraction-engine/logs/sync_status_to_mosaic.log 2>&1

# Carry this machine's locally staged verdicts into our own
# agentic_extraction_status. Off the per-guid path for the same reason: several
# machines draining bins for hours were taking that table's MERGE lock a dozen
# times an hour between them. run_mosaic_structured.py stages verdicts locally
# now (extraction/core/status_staging.py); this is what actually applies them.
#
# A guid whose verdict hasn't synced yet just gets reprocessed on the next
# drain -- more work, not wrong work.
0 */4 * * * PROJECT_ID=cio-mosaic-analytics-pr-853ae3 PYTHONPATH=/home/jupyter/agentic-extraction-engine /opt/micromamba/bin/python3 /home/jupyter/agentic-extraction-engine/scripts/sync_agentic_status.py --apply >> /home/jupyter/agentic-extraction-engine/logs/sync_agentic_status.log 2>&1

# Share Tool 3's schema/code cache across the three machines draining the
# mosaic backlog in parallel. Every 5 minutes on purpose, not every 4 hours
# like the two syncs above: the cache key has so few possible values that a
# single machine bootstraps its own complete cache within ~10-15 minutes, so
# a slower sync would arrive too late to ever help. See
# scripts/sync_schema_cache.py's own docstring for the full reasoning.
#
# cd's into the repo first (unlike the two syncs above) because this script's
# --local-db defaults to the relative cache/schema_code_cache.db -- cron starts
# in $HOME, so without the cd it fails with "unable to open database file".
# Same fix works on all three machines since they share this repo path.
*/5 * * * * cd /home/jupyter/agentic-extraction-engine && PROJECT_ID=cio-mosaic-analytics-pr-853ae3 PYTHONPATH=/home/jupyter/agentic-extraction-engine /opt/micromamba/bin/python3 scripts/sync_schema_cache.py --apply >> /home/jupyter/agentic-extraction-engine/logs/sync_schema_cache.log 2>&1

# Install with:
#     crontab scripts/crontab.agentic-extraction
# Inspect with:
#     crontab -l
#
# Paths assume the repo at /home/jupyter/agentic-extraction-engine and the
# interpreter at /opt/micromamba/bin/python3. Edit both if either differs --
# cron will not find them from a PATH or a shell profile, because it runs
# neither.
